      "lineAnnotations": {
        "16": {"synopsis":"RST $10: prints the character in A through the current channel (CURCHL), by PRINT_A_CHAN.","comment":"PRINT_A_CHAN"},
        "19": {"comment":"Unused ($FF)"},
        "20": {"comment":"$FC here ($FF in the 48K ROM), never run"},
        "1132": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code $0A (report B, \"ENTERO EXCEDE MARGEN\")."},
        "1541": {"synopsis":"SAVE, LOAD, VERIFY and MERGE (class $0B; T_ADDR - $E0 tells which: 0 SAVE, 1 LOAD, 2 VERIFY,\n3 MERGE):\n1. The name (a string, CLASS_A) into a 17-byte header in the workspace (34 for the others:\n   the second 17 take the headers read): the type byte, the name padded to 10 with spaces,\n   or $FF for an empty one (any name). SAVE needs 1-10 characters (report F); the others cut\n   a longer one to 10.\n2. What follows: DATA name() (an array, types 1 and 2), SCREEN$ (type 3, 6912 bytes from\n   $4000), CODE start,length (type 3), or a program (type 0, LINE n for SAVE), into the\n   header: length, start or LINE, and the program's length.\n3. SAVE_CONTROL for SAVE; otherwise LOAD_HEADER_LOOP.\nObserved: SAVE \"\" and SAVE \"abcdefghijk\" gave \"F Invalid file name\"; SAVE \"a\" CODE was\nrefused when checking (on the 48K ROM)."},
        "1995": {"synopsis":"VERIFY, and LOAD of CODE: a wanted length (when not 0) must not be shorter than the block's\n(report R), and only CODE may be longer; the start is the wanted one, or the header's when\n0. Then LOAD_BLOCK, verifying for VERIFY.\nObserved: LOAD \"\" CODE loaded 1,2,3,4 at 32768; LOAD \"abc\" CODE 40000 at 40000; VERIFY with\none byte different and LOAD \"\" CODE 50000,4 for an 8-byte block gave \"R Tape loading error\"\n(on the 48K ROM)."},
        "2054": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code $1A (report R, \"ERROR CARGANDO CINTA\")."},
        "2416": {"synopsis":"SAVE: \"PREPARE LA CINTA Y PULSE ENTER.\" in the lower screen (TAPE_MESSAGES), a key\n(WAIT_KEY), the header (17 bytes, flag 0, SA_BYTES), a gap of 50 interrupts, then the data\n(flag $FF)."},
        "2422": {"comment":"Message 0: \"PREPARE LA CINTA Y PULSE ENTER.\""},
        "2465": {"synopsis":"Tape messages, for PRINT_MESSAGE (read from $0977), in Spanish: entry 0 is empty ($80); then\n\"PREPARE LA CINTA Y PULSE ENTER.\", and, each after a $0D, \"PROGRAMA: \", \"MATRIZ NUM.: \",\n\"MATRIZ LITERAL: \" and \"BYTES:  \"."},
        "2496": {"synopsis":"Read as a table from here (LOAD_HEADER_SHOW, DE = $09C0): entry 0 is the last byte of\n\"PREPARE LA CINTA Y PULSE ENTER.\", entries 1-4 the kinds of file, so type n prints entry n +\n1."},
        "2898": {"synopsis":"$90 and up: first OUT_NEW_TOKENS, for $A3 and $A4 (SPECTRUM and PLAY in +3 BASIC); then as\nin the 48K ROM: $90-$A4 the UDG A - $90, from UDG (OUT_CHAR_BC), $A5 and up OUT_TOKEN.","comment":"$A3/$A4 first (OUT_NEW_TOKENS)"},
        "2901": {"comment":"Filler: the rest of the replaced instructions"},
        "3095": {"synopsis":"PRINT_ENTRY after FIND_ENTRY: OUT_NEW_TOKENS comes here with DE at its own keyword and the\nspacing number on the stack.","comment":"A $20 or more and a letter first?"},
        "3097": {"comment":"A space"},
        "3099": {"comment":"FLAGS bit 0 set: no space"},
        "3157": {"synopsis":"Checks that the line B the next character goes on is on the screen, scrolling when it is\nnot; returns through SET_PRINT_POS. Nothing for the printer.\n1. Upper screen: a line inside the lower screen stops with report 5; the line just below the\n   upper screen scrolls: an automatic listing stops there once the current line is shown\n   (BREG), returning from AUTO_LIST (SP = LIST_SP); otherwise SCR_CT counts down, and at 0\n   the \"]MAS?\" prompt waits for a key (OUT_SCR_COUNT), then OUT_SCR_UPPER.\n2. Lower screen: OUT_SCR_LOWER grows it.\nObserved: printing 30 lines from a cleared screen stopped at the prompt's WAIT_KEY with\nSCR_CT set to 22."},
        "3208": {"synopsis":"SCR_CT one less; at 0, \"]MAS?\": SCR_CT = $18 - B for the next time, the message in the lower\nscreen (stream -3, SCROLL_MESSAGE), a key (WAIT_KEY). SPACE, STOP ($E2) or N stop with\nreport D (REPORT_D); any other key scrolls on, the colours and stream -2 back."},
        "3232": {"comment":"Message 0: \"]MAS?\""},
        "3320": {"synopsis":"The scroll message for PRINT_MESSAGE: entry 0 empty ($80), entry 1 \"]MAS?\" and two spaces;\nthis ROM's character $5D is an inverted question mark, so it shows as a question in Spanish."},
        "3328": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code $0C (report D, \"BREAK/CONT REPITE\")."},
        "3756": {"synopsis":"COPY: the screen's 176 pixel rows go to the printer one by one (PRINTER_ROW), with\ninterrupts off; then the motor stops and the printer buffer is emptied (PRINTER_OFF).\nObserved: with no printer attached (port $FB reads $FF) COPY ended at once with 0 OK (on the\n48K ROM)."},
        "4097": {"synopsis":"Cursor down while INPUT runs: ERR_NR = $10 (report H, \"STOP EN INPUT\") and the editing ends\n(KEY_ENTER)."},
        "4633": {"synopsis":"RAMTOP = HL (the byte below the UDGs on a cold start, the old RAMTOP on NEW). CHARS = $3C00\n(the character set at $3D00 less 256). The machine stack goes just below RAMTOP, whose byte\ngets $3E, and ERR_SP two bytes below SP. Then IM 1, IY = $5C3A (ERR_NR, the base the ROM\nreaches system variables from) and interrupts on.","comment":"RAMTOP = HL"},
        "4636": {"comment":"CHARS = $3C00"},
        "4642": {"comment":"HL = RAMTOP"},
        "4645": {"comment":"$3E under the stack"},
        "4647": {"comment":"Below it"},
        "4648": {"comment":"The machine stack"},
        "4649": {"comment":"Two below"},
        "4651": {"comment":"ERR_SP"},
        "4654": {"comment":"Interrupt mode 1"},
        "4656": {"comment":"IY = ERR_NR"},
        "4660": {"comment":"Interrupts on"},
        "4661": {"comment":"CHANS = $5CB6, the byte after the system variables"},
        "4667": {"comment":"Copy CHANNEL_DATA there"},
        "4670": {"comment":"21 bytes"},
        "4673": {"comment":"DE = CHANS, HL = the data"},
        "4674": {"comment":"Copied"},
        "4676": {"comment":"HL = past it"},
        "4677": {"comment":"DATADD = the channel area's $80"},
        "4681": {"comment":"PROG = VARS = the byte after it, which gets $80: no program, no variables"},
        "4690": {"comment":"E_LINE: an empty edit line ($0D, then $80)"},
        "4700": {"comment":"WORKSP = STKBOT = STKEND: no workspace, an empty calculator stack"},
        "4709": {"comment":"$38: white paper, black ink, for ATTR_P, ATTR_T and BORDCR"},
        "4720": {"comment":"REPDEL = $23, REPPER = $05"},
        "4726": {"comment":"KSTATE ($5C00) and KSTATE + 4 = $FF: both key sets unused"},
        "4732": {"comment":"Copy STREAM_DATA to STRMS"},
        "4738": {"comment":"14 bytes"},
        "4743": {"comment":"FLAGS bit 1 set, so CLEAR_PRBUFF sets the printer's position"},
        "4747": {"comment":"The printer buffer emptied"},
        "4750": {"comment":"DF_SZ = 2"},
        "4754": {"comment":"CLS"},
        "4757": {"comment":"Message 0 of START_MESSAGES: the copyright line"},
        "4758": {"comment":"DE = START_MESSAGES ($1546)"},
        "4761": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "4764": {"comment":"TV_FLAG bit 5 set"},
        "4768": {"comment":"On to the main loop"},
        "4867": {"synopsis":"Ends a direct command, and through the ERR_SP slot every error in one (ERROR_L's RET):\n1. Waits for an interrupt (HALT); prints the printer buffer when it holds anything (FLAGS2\n   bit 1, PRBUFF_OUT).\n2. PRINT_REPORT prints the report on the bottom line as \"<code> <message>,\n   <line>:<statement>\", the code from ERR_NR + 1 (0 when ERR_NR is $FF).\n3. Sets the CONTINUE position (SET_OLDPPC) and goes back to MAIN_ENTRY.\nObserved: PRINT 1 gives \"0 OK, 0:1\", PRINT 1/0 \"6 Number too big, 0:1\", RUN on 10 STOP \"9\nSTOP statement, 10:1\" (on the 48K ROM)."},
        "4924": {"synopsis":"Prints the report's code character (PRINT_A_DIGIT), a space, then its message; then\nHOOK_REPORT, which in this version always does what it replaced (no hook into the other\nROM).","comment":"Printed"},
        "4927": {"comment":"A space"},
        "4930": {"comment":"A = the number"},
        "4931": {"comment":"The message for the number, from REPORT_MESSAGES"},
        "4937": {"comment":"Message 0, DE = $1536 (HOOK_REPORT)"},
        "4940": {"comment":"Filler: the rest of the replaced instructions"},
        "4944": {"comment":"The line number, PPC ($FFFE for a direct command prints as 0)"},
        "4951": {"comment":"':'"},
        "4954": {"comment":"The statement number, SUBPPC"},
        "4959": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "4962": {"comment":"Empty the edit line, keeping its $0D"},
        "4965": {"comment":"Report 0: no CONTINUE position"},
        "4971": {"comment":"Reports 9 (STOP statement) and L (BREAK into program) continue after the statement"},
        "4975": {"comment":"Report L?"},
        "5009": {"synopsis":"Report messages, in Spanish, in the keyword table's form, for PRINT_MESSAGE. Entry 0 is\nempty ($80), entries 1-28 are the texts of reports 0-9 and A-R, \"OK\" to \"ERROR CARGANDO\nCINTA\". PRINT_REPORT prints the one for the report's number. Being longer than the English\ntexts, they end at $1543, so COMMA_MESSAGES is at $1544 and START_MESSAGES at $1546."},
        "5444": {"synopsis":"A table of its own from here: entry 0 is the last byte of \"ERROR CARGANDO CINTA\", entry 1 is\n\", \", whose final space is START_MESSAGES' entry 0. HOOK_REPORT still loads DE with $1536, a\nplace inside \"ERROR CARGANDO CINTA\": PRINT_MESSAGE skips to the end of that entry first, so\nentry 1 is \", \" all the same.\nObserved: PRINT 1/0 in 48 BASIC gave \"6 NUMERO MUY GRANDE, 0:1\"."},
        "5446": {"synopsis":"Start-up messages, for PRINT_MESSAGE: entry 0 is a lone space, entry 1 the copyright line\n(the $7F character and \" 1982 Amstrad\"), which start-up prints as message 0 (from $1296)."},
        "5588": {"synopsis":"Waits for a key from the current channel: calls its input routine (CHAN_INPUT) until one\ncomes (carry). Sets TV_FLAG bit 3 first unless bit 5 is set. An input routine giving NZ and\nno carry stops with error code 7 (report 8, \"FIN DE FICHERO\").\nExit: A = the key."},
        "5925": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code $17 (report O, \"CANAL NO VALIDO\").\nObserved: FORMAT \"a\" gave \"O Invalid stream, 0:1\" (on the 48K ROM)."},
        "5981": {"synopsis":"The channel's name, one letter, either case: its offset from OPEN_LETTERS (DE = 1, 6 or 16);\nan empty name, another letter or a longer name is report F.\nObserved: OPEN #5,\"q\", OPEN #5,\"ss\" and OPEN #5,\"\" gave \"F Invalid file name\" (on the 48K\nROM)."},
        "5989": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code $0E (report F, \"NOMBRE INCORRECTO\")."},
        "7030": {"synopsis":"Where a command returns to: BREAK_KEY first (report L for BREAK); then, with no jump (NSPPC\nbit 7 set), the next statement (STMT_NEXT); otherwise the jump: to the edit line (NEWPPC's\nbit 15 set, RUN_EDIT_LINE) or a program line (LINE_NEW).\nObserved: CAPS SHIFT + SPACE during 30 GO TO 30 gave \"L BREAK into program, 30:1\" (on the\n48K ROM)."},
        "7070": {"synopsis":"Goes to line NEWPPC, statement NSPPC: the line found (FIND_LINE) when it is there; a missing\nline asked for with a statement stops with report N; a missing line otherwise runs the next\none, or, past the program, stops with report 0 (error code $FF).\nObserved: RUN on 10 PRINT 5: GO TO 30 / 20 PRINT 6 printed 5 and reported \"0 OK, 10:2\" (on\nthe 48K ROM)."},
        "7148": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code $16 (report N, \"SENT. PERDIDA\")."},
        "7214": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code 1 (report 2, \"VARIABLE NO DEFINIDA\"): a missing array."},
        "7306": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code $0B (report C, \"SIN SENTIDO EN BASIC\")."},
        "7556": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code $11 (report I, \"FOR SIN NEXT\").\nObserved: FOR k=5 TO 1: PRINT k with no NEXT gave report I."},
        "7640": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code 0 (report 1, \"NEXT SIN FOR\")."},
        "7661": {"synopsis":"READ: for each variable (CLASS_1), when running, the next DATA item: the one at DATADD after\na ',', or the first of the next DATA statement (LOOK_PROG for $E4); none is report E. It is\nevaluated with the variable's type and assigned (VAL_FETCH), and DATADD moves past it;\nCH_ADD comes back to the READ statement (kept in X_PTR).\nObserved: 10 READ a,b$: PRINT a;b$: READ c / 20 DATA 5,\"q\" printed 5q and then gave \"E Out\nof DATA, 10:3\" (on the 48K ROM)."},
        "7808": {"synopsis":"POKE: stores the byte at the address (TWO_PARAM: A the byte, BC the address).\nObserved: POKE 30001,-1 stored 255; POKE 30001,300 was report B (on the 48K ROM)."},
        "7839": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code $0A (report B, \"ENTERO EXCEDE MARGEN\")."},
        "7898": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code $15 (report M, \"RAMTOP INCORRECTA\")."},
        "7971": {"synopsis":"RETURN: takes the statement and line GO SUB kept from below the ERR_SP slot, moves the error\naddress and ERR_SP up, and jumps there (GO_TO_2). Reaching the $3E marker under RAMTOP\ninstead is report 7.\nObserved: RETURN with no GO SUB gave \"7 RETURN without GOSUB\" (on the 48K ROM)."},
        "7990": {"synopsis":"Everything back on the stack; stops with error code 6 (report 7, \"RETURN SIN GOSUB\")."},
        "8656": {"synopsis":"STOP: report H (error code $10) when running.\nObserved: STOP answered to INPUT n gave \"H STOP in INPUT, 10:1\" (on the 48K ROM)."},
        "8721": {"synopsis":"Sets a temporary colour or effect: control code A ($10-$15) with value D, from\nSCREEN_OUTPUT's OUT_OPERANDS.\n1. INK and PAPER (COL_INK_PAPER): 0-7 into ATTR_T; 8 keeps the screen's (MASK_T); 9 a\n   contrasting colour (P_FLAG bit 4 or 6, which OUT_ATTR applies); 10 or more is report K.\n2. FLASH and BRIGHT (COL_FLASH_BRIGHT): 0 or 1 into ATTR_T bit 7 or 6; 8 keeps the screen's;\n   anything else report K.\n3. INVERSE and OVER: 0 or 1 into P_FLAG bit 2 or 0; anything else report K.\nObserved: PAPER 1; INK 9 printed x on $0F, PAPER 6; INK 9 y on $30; INK 8; PAPER 8; BRIGHT 1\nover a PAPER 2 cell gave $50; INK 10, FLASH 2 and BORDER 8 gave \"K Invalid colour\" (on the\n48K ROM)."},
        "8772": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code $13 (report K, \"COLOR NO VALIDO\")."},
        "9465": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code $0A (report B, \"ENTERO EXCEDE MARGEN\"); TAKE_BYTE_SIGN jumps here for\na number over 255."},
        "9929": {"synopsis":"A variable: LOOK_VARS, report 2 when it is not there; subscripts or slicing\n(VAR_SUBSCRIPTS); a number's 5 bytes are stacked (PUSH_NUMBER) when running.\nObserved: PRINT zz with no zz gave \"2 Variable not found\" (on the 48K ROM)."},
        "10379": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code $19 (report Q, \"PARAMETRO ERRONEO\")."},
        "10784": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code 2 (report 3, \"SUBINDICE INCORRECTO\")."},
        "12717": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code 5 (report 6, \"NUMERO MUY GRANDE\").\nObserved: 1/0 gave it."},
        "13543": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code 9 (report A, \"ARG. INVALIDO\")."},
        "14083": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code 5 (report 6, \"NUMERO MUY GRANDE\")."},
        "14099": {"synopsis":"ln ($25): the natural logarithm; x of 0 or less stops with error code 9 (report A, \"ARG.\nINVALIDO\"):\n1. x split into its binary exponent e (exponent byte - 128) and mantissa m (exponent byte\n   $80, 0.5 to 1); m of 0.8 or less is doubled and e lessened by 1 (m then 0.8 to 1.6).\n2. ln x = e x ln 2 (0.693147) + (m - 1) x series-0C of 2.5 (m - 1) - 0.5 (CALC_SERIES).\nObserved: LN 1 0, LN 10 2.3025851; LN 0 report A."},
        "14889": {"synopsis":"REPORT_CHAR's hook: FLAGS bit 4 tested, but the jump that would follow it is two NOPs, so it\nalways does what it replaced: A = 0 and DE = $1536, COMMA_MESSAGES' place in the English\nROM, inside the last report's text here (see COMMA_MESSAGES)."},
        "14895": {"comment":"A = 0, DE = $1536"},
        "15511": {"synopsis":"Unused: $00 up to the character set."},
        "15616": {"synopsis":"Character set: the pictures of the 96 character codes $20-$7F, 8 bytes each, 768 bytes up to\nthe ROM's end. A byte is one pixel row, top row first, bit 7 the leftmost pixel; code c's\npicture is at CHARACTER_SET + (c - $20) x 8, which is CHARS + c x 8 with CHARS = $3C00\n(SET_RAMTOP). Three readers: - printing: OUT_CHAR draws code c from CHARS + c x 8, on the\nscreen or into the printer buffer, so pointing CHARS elsewhere replaces the set; - SCREEN$:\nSCREENS_VALUE compares a screen cell with the 96 pictures from CHARS + $100, plain and\ninverted; - start-up: RAM_TOP_FOUND (at $1203) copies the pictures of A to U ($3E08-$3EAF)\nas the 21 UDGs. Codes $80-$8F (block graphics), $90-$A4 (UDGs) and $A5 up (keywords) have no\npictures here. $20 - Character: ' ' In this Spanish ROM five pictures differ from the 48K\nROM's: $5B inverted exclamation mark, $5C N with tilde, $5D inverted question mark, $60 Pt,\n$7C n with tilde."},
        "15624": {"synopsis":"$21 - Character: '!'"},
        "15632": {"synopsis":"$22 - Character: '\"'"},
        "15640": {"synopsis":"$23 - Character: '#'"},
        "15648": {"synopsis":"$24 - Character: '$'"},
        "15656": {"synopsis":"$25 - Character: '%'"},
        "15664": {"synopsis":"$26 - Character: '&'"},
        "15672": {"synopsis":"$27 - Character: apostrophe"},
